# OpenSocrates for Grok Build

This native Grok Build plugin contains one user-visible `opensocrates` skill
and {{METHOD_COUNT}} internal authored procedures. Grok may select the skill in
the same turn through its native skill-selection surface, and users can invoke
it explicitly with `/opensocrates`.

When Grok reads a selected generated method, its complete procedure begins with
three authored teacher questions for the active agent to settle before using the
remaining procedure as a check. These questions are native skill content; this
package does not claim OpenSocrates hook injection.

The package is content-only: it contains no hooks, MCP server, agent, command,
launcher, native runtime, or nested model selector. It uses the current Grok
Build model and authentication without requiring another API key or hardcoded
model ID.

The complete procedure, including its leading teacher questions, must be read in
the current conversation before a method may be applied, named, or cited.

